# Variables substituted at container start: PUBLIC_HOSTNAME (server_name, no port) and
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN (scheme://host[:port], as browsers see it). Both are required; the container
# entrypoint substitutes only variables that exist in its environment, and compose marks them required.

upstream running_tracker_api {
  server api:3000;
  keepalive 16;
}

# Plain HTTP only redirects, always to the configured origin: the Host header is never echoed.
server {
  listen 80 default_server;
  server_name _;

  # Liveness for the container health check only: no data, no upstream.
  location = /healthz {
    access_log off;
    default_type text/plain;
    return 200 "ok";
  }

  location / {
    return 301 ${PUBLIC_ORIGIN}$request_uri;
  }
}

# A TLS client asking for any other name is refused during the handshake.
server {
  listen 443 ssl default_server;
  http2 on;
  ssl_reject_handshake on;
}

server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  http2 on;
  server_name ${PUBLIC_HOSTNAME};

  ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/fullchain.pem;
  ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/tls/privkey.pem;
  ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
  ssl_prefer_server_ciphers off;
  ssl_session_timeout 10m;
  ssl_session_cache shared:TLS:1m;
  ssl_session_tickets off;

  root /usr/share/nginx/html;
  index index.html;
  client_max_body_size 128k;

  include /etc/nginx/snippets/security-headers.conf;

  # Live SSE: same no-buffer / no-cache / no-compression / no-retry policy as the verified
  # transport profile (ADR-0026).
  location ~ ^/api/orgs/[^/]+/live/?$ {
    include /etc/nginx/snippets/security-headers.conf;
    proxy_pass http://running_tracker_api;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Connection "";
    proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $http_host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_set_header Accept-Encoding "";

    proxy_connect_timeout 5s;
    proxy_send_timeout 30s;
    proxy_read_timeout 75s;
    send_timeout 30s;

    proxy_request_buffering off;
    proxy_buffering off;
    proxy_cache off;
    proxy_next_upstream off;
    gzip off;
    proxy_pass_header X-Accel-Buffering;
  }

  location ~* ^/api/auth/login/?$ {
    include /etc/nginx/snippets/security-headers.conf;
    limit_req zone=oidc_login burst=4 nodelay;
    limit_req_status 429;
    proxy_pass http://running_tracker_api;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Connection "";
    proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
    # Overwrite, never append untrusted client-supplied identity headers.
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_connect_timeout 5s;
    proxy_send_timeout 30s;
    proxy_read_timeout 30s;
    proxy_next_upstream off;
    proxy_cache off;
  }

  location /api/ {
    include /etc/nginx/snippets/security-headers.conf;
    proxy_pass http://running_tracker_api;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Connection "";
    proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $http_host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_connect_timeout 5s;
    proxy_send_timeout 30s;
    proxy_read_timeout 30s;
    proxy_next_upstream off;
    proxy_cache off;
  }

  # Vite emits content-hashed file names under /assets/.
  location /assets/ {
    include /etc/nginx/snippets/security-headers.conf;
    add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable" always;
    try_files $uri =404;
  }

  location / {
    include /etc/nginx/snippets/security-headers.conf;
    add_header Cache-Control "no-cache" always;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
  }
}
